-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",60,{
[1889]="70034446\n1\tTalk to Horn\030Talk to Corudan\tHorn and Corudan are in Nona's cave, and you should speak to them about the day's journey.\n2\tTalk to Nona and travel to Byre Tor\tNona is in her cave in the High Knolls, preparing to depart for Byre Tor.\n3\tTalk to Corudan\tYou have narrowly survived an encounter with Núrzum and should now speak to Corudan in Nona's cave.\n",
[1890]="70034447\n1\tFind the glade of the oldest Ent in Balewood\tSomewhere in the Balewood, an old Ent sleeps. Only he will have the authority to order an attack upon Núrzum.\n2\tTalk to Corudan in Leaflock's mead\tYou and Corudan have stumbled upon the glade of an ancient and very tired Ent.\n3\tTalk to the Ent and ask him for help against Núrzum\tYou have come to Balewood to petition Leaflock the Ent for help against Núrzum.\n4\tTalk to Corudan in Leaflock's mead\tCorudan is in Leaflock's mead, in Balewood.\n",
[1891]="7000A8A8\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan is in his room in the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Laerdan's room is atop the stairs through the door on your right as you enter the keep. Golodir has given you a finely-woven cloth bag that was used to cover the palantír at Carn Dûm when it was not in use. He also cautioned you not to touch the palantír with your hands and to warn Laerdan not to underestimate your enemy.\n2\tCollect Laerdan's Note\tA note from Laerdan is pinned to the door of his room in the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. You have returned from Gath Forthnír with a finely-woven cloth bag with which you can carry the palantír, but Laerdan seems to have gone. However, he left a note for you on his door.\n3\tTalk to Tadan\tRanger Tadan is in the prison atop the stairs through the door on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Laerdan has left a note for you on his door, indicating that he has gone to Barad Tironn to confront Amarthiel by himself. You should show this note to Tadan at once.\n4\tTalk to Mordrambor\tMordrambor is in the prison atop the stairs through the door on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Ranger Tadan told you that Laerdan asked to guard the prisoner for a time while Tadan enjoyed a respite from the stifling air of the prison. In that time, Tadan believes that Mordrambor worked some foul sorcery on Laerdan that caused the Elf to venture to Barad Tironn alone. You should speak with Mordrambor about this treachery.\n5\tBring Laerdan's note to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Mordrambor has revealed his purpose to you: to send Laerdan to Amarthiel in Barad Tironn and to keep you occupied with trivial tasks in Annúminas and Evendim while his mistress made use of the palantír in her possession. You must deliver these unpleasant tidings to Calenglad.\n",
[1892]="7000A8A9\n1\tTalk to Calenglad and travel into Barad Tironn in search of the palantír\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Calenglad is waiting to hear that your allies are prepared for the assault on Barad Tironn and the reclamation of the palantír. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. The palantír has been recovered, but Laerdan was left to an uncertain fate in the depths of Barad Tironn and Amarthiel saw what she sought in the depths of the seeing-stone.\n",
[1893]="70034448\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Balewood, and be noisy about it (total: 5)\tOrcs can be found in Balewood, especially along the path called Núrzum's Wrath.\n2\tTalk to Leaflock\tYou have raised quite a din fighting Orcs in Balewood, and should see if it was enough to waken Leaflock.\n3\tDefeat Orcs in Balewood, and be even noisier about it (total: 5)\tOrcs can be found in Balewood, especially along the path called Núrzum's Wrath.\n4\tTalk to Leaflock\tYou have raised quite a din fighting Orcs in Balewood, and should see if it was enough to waken Leaflock.\n5\tTalk to Corudan\tCorudan is in Leaflock's mead, trying to devise a means of waking the slumbering Ent.\n6\tCollect White Hand helmet from an Uruk in Balewood\030Collect a White Hand blade from an Uruk in Balewood\tWhite Hand Uruks can be found at Núrzum's Wrath, in Balewood. Corudan thinks you should collect some White Hand equipment from Uruks in Balewood and show them to Leaflock.\n7\tShow the White Hand equipment to Leaflock the Ent\tYou have collected some White Hand equipment from Orcs in Balewood and should show them to Leaflock. That may rouse the Ent to wakefulness.\n8\tTalk to Leaflock\tYou are trying to waken Leaflock to your cause.\n9\tTalk to Leaflock\tYou are trying to waken Leaflock to your cause.\n10\tTalk to Leaflock\tYou are trying to waken Leaflock to your cause.\n11\tTalk to Corudan in Leaflock's mead\tCorudan is in Leaflock's mead.\n12\tTalk to Corudan back in Nona's cave\tCorudan has agreed to meet you back at Nona's cave after he is done speaking with Leaflock.\n",
[1894]="70034449\n1\tTalk to Gléowine\tGléowine is in Nona's cave, and you should speak to him to see how things have been while you and Corudan sought out Leaflock.\n2\tTalk to Horn\tHorn is in Nona's cave, and you should speak to him.\n3\tTalk to Horn when you are ready to eat\tHorn is in Nona's cave, waiting to speak with you when you are ready to take your meal.\n4\tTalk to Nona\tNona is in her cave in the High Knolls.\n",
[1895]="70034032\n1\tDefeat Saruman's mounted minions in the Sutcrofts ([see journal]/5)\tSaruman's mounted minions threaten the people of Rohan throughout the Sutcrofts. Horn and Corudan think you should make the most of your exile from Edoras by continuing to combat Saruman's mounted minions in East Rohan.\n2\tDefeat Saruman's mounted minions in the Sutcrofts (4/5)\tSaruman's mounted minions threaten the people of Rohan throughout the Sutcrofts. Horn and Corudan think you should make the most of your exile from Edoras by continuing to combat Saruman's mounted minions in East Rohan.\n3\tBring the battered harp to Horn at the crossing of the Entwash, in the Sutcrofts\tHorn is at the crossing of the Entwash, in the Sutcrofts, and he will wish to see the battered harp you found.\n",
[1896]="7000A86E\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan has been given a room in the keep on the island of Tinnudir. His room is atop a flight of stairs on the right as you enter the keep. Calenglad has told you that Laerdan the Elf has come to Tinnudir bearing information that might help you combat Amarthiel's forces in Annúminas. He said that Laerdan asked for you by name.\n2\tBring Laerdan's letter to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Laerdan has written a letter to Calenglad explaining the threat Amarthiel poses. He has asked you to read the letter and deliver it to Calenglad.\n",
[1897]="700340D7\n1\tGuards at the entrance of Snowbourn or its stables may have seen Gléowine, if he lives. Horn hopes that his master Gléowine found his way safely to Snowbourn, despite much evidence to the contrary.\t\n2\tSearch for Gléowine near the barracks in Snowbourn\tThe guard with whom you spoke did not recognize Gléowine from your description, but advised you to look for him near the barracks in Snowbourn, where many of the recent arrivals in the city have congregated.\n3\tTalk to Gléowine by the barracks in Snowbourn\tYou have found Gléowine in Snowbourn, but he is very drunk.\n4\tTalk to Alhild, near Gléowine at the barracks\tAlhild is near Gléowine by the barracks in Snowbourn. You have found Gléowine, but you need him to sober up before he will be of any use to anyone. Perhaps Alhild can be of help.\n5\tCollect a Snowbourn honeycomb\030Obtain a bladder of water from Heiu\030Collect a handful of Snowbourn almonds\030Pick some swamp cabbage (total: 4)\tAlhild knows where around Snowbourn to collect the ingredients for the various drunkenness remedies she mentioned. You need to collect the ingredients necessary to relieve Gléowine's drunkenness.\n6\tGive the honey, water, almonds, and cabbage to Gléowine to ease his drunken state\tGléowine is by the barracks in Snowbourn. You have obtained the ingredients for several drunkenness remedies and should now apply them to Gléowine in order to sober him up.\n7\tTalk to Horn by the barracks in Snowbourn\tHorn is by his master Gléowine, outside the barracks in Snowbourn. You have found Gléowine and attempted to ease his drunkenness with Alhild's remedies, but none of them seem to have worked. Now Horn wants to speak with you.\n",
[1898]="7000A86F\n1\tTalk to Rosselloth\tRosselloth is in the courtyard of Gwaelband. Gwaelband is west of Men Erain, beyond Minathranc, at the front entrance of Annúminas. Calenglad has decided that Amarthiel's forces should be engaged in Annúminas in order to keep her from focusing her attention upon the palantír. He has sent you to speak with Rosselloth for advice on what you can do to help.\n2\tTalk to Fainneleg\tThe Ranger Fainneleg is at Echad Garthadir, a small camp south-west of Gwaelband, on a higher level of the city. If the Rangers hold Gwaelband, the gate provides easy access to the higher level. Otherwise, you will need to swim west past the Port of Annúminas to Gaerannon and then climb through the city to reach Echad Garthadir. Rosselloth has told you to speak with Fainneleg, the Ranger organizing the defence of Annúminas.\n",
[1899]="70034117\n1\tTalk to Gléowine by the barracks in Snowbourn\tGléowine is by the barracks in Snowbourn. Gléowine has been brought back to sobriety by something, and seems ready to talk to you.\n2\tTalk to Corudan by the barracks in Snowbourn\030Talk to Horn by the barracks in Snowbourn\tHorn and Corudan are by the barracks in Snowbourn. Gléowine wants to travel with you to investigate what has happened in Wildermore, but first he needs some of the possessions he gave away while in the depths of his despair.\n3\tTalk to Arnwi by the south gate of Snowbourn\tOne of the children of Snowbourn may know where to find Gléowine's map. Gléowine wishes to travel with you to investigate the curious silence that has enveloped Wildermore, but first he wants you to recover the map he abandoned.\n4\tFind Britred south of Snowbourn\tBritred left on an adventure by the south gate of Snowbourn. How far south did he get on his quest? You were told that Britred took Gléowine's map and went on an adventure. If you find him, he may return the map to you.\n5\tBring the map to Gléowine by the barracks in Snowbourn\tGléowine is by the barracks in Snowbourn. You have recovered Gléowine's map and should return it to him.\n6\tTalk to Horn by the barracks in Snowbourn\tHorn is by the barracks in Snowbourn. You have returned Gléowine's map and should now speak with Horn about your preparations to travel to Wildermore.\n7\tTalk to Aldor Harding in the Mead Hall of Harwick, in the Wold\tAldor Harding is in the Mead Hall of Harwick, in the Wold. Fastred has no men to spare in an investigation of Wildermore, and has sent you to give Harding the unfortunate tidings.\n8\tTalk to Gléowine outside the Mead Hall of Harwick, in the Wold\tGléowine is on the wooden porch outside the Mead Hall in Harwick, in the Wold. Gléowine wishes to speak with you.\n",
[1900]="7000A87D\n1\tTalk to Gwonil and help defend her position\030Talk to Torchirion and defend his position\030Defeat Bow-wielding Angmarim in Annúminas (total: 8)\tGwonil is on the docks at the Port of Annúminas, north of Echad Garthadir. Torchirion is at Adannon, a small gate in the city wall west of the docks that provides access to the western shore of Lake Nenuial. Angmarim archers lie in wait throughout the city, often in hiding. Fainneleg has asked you to hurry to the defence of Gwonil and of Torchirion, for he fears that these Rangers cannot withstand another assault on their positions. He also wishes you to defeat any bow-wielding Angmarim you come across within the city.\n2\tTalk to Fainneleg\tFainneleg is at Echad Garthadir, the Ranger-camp on the middle level of Annúminas. You have spoken with Gwonil and Torchirion and defeated several bow-wielding Angmarim in Annúminas and should return now to Fainneleg to report of your victories.\n",
[1901]="70034118\n1\tTalk to Horn outside the Mead Hall in Harwick\tHorn is standing by Gléowine on the porch outside the Mead Hall of Harwick. You should speak with Horn about your journey into Wildermore.\n2\tTravel to the town of Scylfig, in the Writhendowns of Wildermore\tThe town of Scylfig is located in the Writhendowns, in Wildermore, west of the Wold. Your companions have agreed that it is time to begin your search for Harding's men in Wildermore. You will begin with the town of Scylfig.\n3\tFind Wídfara or Léodwig within Scylfig, if they are to be found\tWídfara may be within the town of Scylfig, in the Writhendowns area of Wildermore. If Wídfara is within Scylfig, you should find him and learn why he has not returned to the Wold.\n4\tFind the White Hand camp in the south-east\030Find the possibly-haunted fishing town\030Find Thrymm's training camp\030Defeat mounted combat foes in the Writhendowns (total: 5)\tThe White Hand has established a camp in the south-east corner of the Writhendowns. The abandoned fishing village can be found to the north-west of Scylfig. Thrymm Red-beard's training camp is to the east of Scylfig. Wídfara has agreed to tell you more of what happened in Wildermore if you help the people of the Writhendowns by facing down their foes near three significant locations.\n5\tTalk to Wídfara\tWídfara is in Scylfig, in the Writhendowns. You have done as he asked, and should now return to Wídfara to hear more of his tale.\n6\tTalk to Corudan in Scylfig\tCorudan is in Scylfig. Corudan listened to Wídfara's tale, and may have some thoughts about it.\n7\tFind Gléowine somewhere within Scylfig\tIt is Corudan's hope that Gléowine remains still within Scylfig. Corudan wants you to find Gléowine if he remains in Scylfig.\n8\tTalk to Horn in Scylfig\tHorn is in Scylfig with Corudan and Wídfara. You have comforted Gléowine and should now speak with Horn in Scylfig.\n",
[1902]="7000A87E\n1\tCollect Orders Recovered from Clorhir\030Collect Orders Recovered from Menelband\030Collect Orders Recovered from Gwaelband\tFainneleg is seeking orders from the Angmarim that occupy the courtyard of Gwaelband, to the north-east of Echad Garthadir, where you encountered Rosselloth; from Clorhir, in front of the pools of Glinghant, east of Echad Garthadir; and at Menelband, on the highest level of the city. Fainneleg has told you of three volatile locations in Annúminas. He wants you to defeat the Angmarim and search their corpses for any orders they may carry. If the Dúnedain hold any of these locations, Fainneleg told you to search for the corpses of any Angmarim that may have been killed in the fighting; they too may have carried such orders.\n2\tBring the orders to Fainneleg\tFainneleg is at the Ranger camp of Echad Garthadir in the centre of Annúminas. You have recovered the orders and should return at once to Fainneleg.\n",
[1903]="7000A87F\n1\tBring sheaf of papers to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir. Fainneleg heard some news from Calenglad that renewed his hope and has sent you to the old Ranger to hear it. He gave you the orders written in the Black Speech you collected from Gwaelband, Clorhir, and Tirband, and said Calenglad might have need for them after all.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad and capture Mordrambor\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir. Calenglad is waiting to hear if you will agree to undertake the dangerous mission to capture Mordrambor, one of Amarthiel's Black Númenórean lieutenants.\n3\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir. You and a contingent of Rangers have captured Mordrambor, one of the Black Númenórean sorcerers sworn to Amarthiel.\n",
[1904]="7003411D\n1\tTalk to Reeve Gárwig in the Mead Hall of Forlaw\tReeve Gárwig rules from within the Mead Hall of Forlaw, on the southernmost shore of the Isingmere. Horn has learned that the people of Wildermore do not have confidence in Reeve Gárwig, and thinks you should visit him and learn his plans.\n2\tDefeat uruk-hai along the shores of the Isingmere (total: 6)\030Burn uruk-hai supply barrels (total: 4)\tThe uruk-hai have a camp on the shore of the Isingmere, and Reeve Gárwig has asked you to burn their supply barrels and thin their number. Reeve Gárwig knows you cannot stand against Núrzum, so he wants you to try and combat some of the uruk-hai instead.\n3\tTalk to Reeve Gárwig in the Mead Hall of Forlaw\tReeve Gárwig is in the Mead Hall of Forlaw, in Wildermore. You have attempted to hinder the movements of the uruk-hai on the shores of the Isingmere, and should return to Reeve Gárwig.\n4\tTalk to Horn outside the Mead Hall of Forlaw\tHorn is outside the Mead Hall of Forlaw. Reeve Gárwig has given up hope, but you are certain Horn has not, and should see what he intends.\n5\tReassure scared villagers in Forlaw that Reeve Gárwig still fights for them (total: 6)\tScared villagers can be found throughout Forlaw. Horn has asked you to reassure the people of Forlaw that their Reeve is working on some means of defeating Núrzum. That this is not exactly true does not seem to worry Horn very much.\n6\tTalk to Horn outside the Mead Hall of Forlaw\tHorn is outside the Mead Hall of Forlaw, in Wildermore. You have reassured scared villagers and should now return to Horn.\n",
[1905]="7003427D\n1\tDefeat Warg-riders in the Fallows (total: 5)\030Defeat foes at the southern exit from Wildermore, in the Fallows (total: 5)\tWarg-riders can be found throughout the Fallows, in Wildermore, and some foe has shut the southern road into the Norcrofts. Horn has asked you to defeat Warg-riders in the Fallows and to investigate the southern road out of Wildermore.\n2\tTalk to Horn at Gárferth's Farm\tHorn is waiting for you at Gárferth's Farm, in the south-east reaches of the Fallows. You have defeated both Warg-riders and the uruk-hai at Kúthaus, and should now meet Horn at Gárferth's Farm, where he said he would be waiting for you.\n3\tDefeat Wargs and their riders in the Fallows (total: 6)\030Collect salvageable crops from Edsig's Farm (total: 4)\tWargs and their riders stalk the Fallows, and many can be located Edsig's Farm, located in the southern reaches. Horn has asked you to defeat the Wargs and their riders in the Fallows, and to bring any salvageable crops you find from Edsig's Farm to the provisioner at Forlaw.\n4\tBring salvaged crops to the provisioner in Forlaw\tThe provisioner of Forlaw is in the southern courtyard of the city. You have salvaged some crops from an overrun farm in the Fallows, and should bring them to the provisioner at Forlaw.\n5\tTalk to Gléowine in Forlaw\tGléowine is in Forlaw, and wishes to speak with you. You have brought some crops to the provisioner in Forlaw, and should now see what Gléowine has been doing.\n",
[1906]="7000A884\n1\tShow sheaf of papers to Mordrambor\tMordrambor is being held prisoner in the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. As you enter the keep, the door on your left leads to stairs that climb up to the prison. Calenglad has given you the orders you collected from the Angmarim in Annúminas, so that you may show them to the Black Númenórean prisoner. Mordrambor will know the Black Speech and must be made to translate the orders for you.\n",
[1907]="7000A885\n1\tFind Amarthiel's emissary to the Gauredain\030Find Amarthiel's emissary to the Kergrim\030Find Amarthiel's emissary to the Men of Rantost\tMordrambor told you of three Angmarim emissaries sent to buy the loyalties of new allies for Amarthiel's armies in Annúminas: the tomb-robbers on the island of Rantost, in the north-east corner of the lake, the Gauredain near the north-west corner of the lake, and the Kergrim among the tombs of Men Erain, along the south-east corner of the lake. Mordrambor has told you of three emissaries sent by boat across Lake Nenuial to buy the loyalties of some of the evils that plague Evendim.\n2\tTalk to Tadan\tRanger Tadan is in the prison atop the flight of stairs on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. You have defeated the three emissaries sent by Amarthiel to recruit new allies for the battle of Annúminas and should now report of your victories to Tadan.\n",
[1908]="700342AC\n1\tTalk to Corudan in Forlaw\030Talk to Horn in Forlaw\tHorn and Corudan are in the town of Forlaw, in Wildermore. Gléowine wants to visit Dunfast, the village in which he was born, to see how it has been affected by this unnatural winter.\n2\tTravel to the village of Dunfast, in the middle of the Whitshaws, in Wildermore\tThe village of Dunfast is located in the middle of the Whitshaws, in Wildermore. Horn and Corudan agree that you should all journey to Gléowine's home, Dunfast, and see how it has been treated by this unnatural winter.\n3\tTalk to Gléowine outside Dunfast\tGléowine is outside the village of Dunfast, in the Whitshaws. Little moves among the houses of Dunfast, and Gléowine is very worried.\n4\tTalk to Gléowine and explore Dunfast together\tGléowine is outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws. Gléowine wants to investigate Dunfast with you, Horn, and Corudan, and is waiting to speak with you.\n5\tTalk to Horn outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws\tHorn is waiting to speak with you outside Dunfast. Nona reappeared again, but the reunion did not proceed as Horn wished. He is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[1909]="700342E9\n1\tTalk to Corudan outside Dunfast\tCorudan is outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws. Horn is of little use to anyone, pining as he is over Nona. Perhaps Corudan will have some guidance.\n2\tDefeat Orcs in the Whitshaws (total: 4)\030Find root vegetables in the Whitshaws (total: 8)\tOrcs can be found throughout the Whitshaws. Root vegetables can be found at the bases of many trees in the area outside Dunfast. Corudan wants you to keep busy while Horn decides what he wants to do, and this involves defeating Saruman's minions in the Whitshaws and collecting the root vegetables Nona mentioned.\n3\tBring root vegetables to Corudan outside Dunfast\tCorudan is outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws. You have done as Corudan asked, defeating Orcs and Warg-riders and collecting the root vegetables for which Nona asked.\n4\tTalk to Horn outside Dunfast\tHorn is outside Dunfast, in the Whitshaws. Corudan has asked that you see how Horn is feeling.\n",
[1910]="7000A88A\n1\tTalk to Mordrambor\tMordrambor is in the prison atop the stairs through the door on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Mordrambor has been muttering about new attacks upon the city, but refuses to give Tadan any further details. Tadan hopes you may be able to get some information from the prisoner.\n2\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan has been given a room in the keep on the island of Tinnudir, atop the stairs behind the door on your right as you enter the keep. Mordrambor has told you that Amarthiel plans renewed assaults on the city of Annúminas, but will only reveal the locations for these new attacks if you deliver a message to Laerdan: 'Laerdan, thy time is soon ended, thy mistakes soon accounted. Amarthiel awaits thee in Barad Tironn, where she will sit in judgement over thee.'\n3\tTalk to Mordrambor\tMordrambor is being held prisoner in the prison atop the stairs on your left as you enter the keep on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. You have delivered Mordrambor's message to Laerdan as he requested, and the Elf told you to beware the Black Númenórean's treachery, for even imprisoned he poses great danger. If he upholds his word, Mordrambor should now tell you the location of Amarthiel's latest planned assault on Annúminas.\n",
[1911]="7000A88B\n1\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. Mordrambor has told you to tell Calenglad of the planned locations for Amarthiel's next assaults: the Port of Annúminas and the gate of Adannon.\n2\tTalk to Gwonil and defend her position\030Talk to Torchirion and defend his position\tGwonil is on the docks at the Port of Annúminas, north of Echad Garthadir. Torchirion is at Adannon, a small gate in the city wall west of the docks that provides access to the western shore of Lake Nenuial. Calenglad has asked you to hurry to the defence of Gwonil and Torchirion; according to the words of Mordrambor, they will bear the brunt of Amarthiel's latest assault upon the city.\n3\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. You have defended Gwonil and Torchirion from the assaults foretold by Mordrambor and should now return to Calenglad with news of your success.\n",
[1912]="70034321\n1\tTravel to the city of Byre Tor, in the High Knolls of Wildermore\tThe City of Byre Tor is in the High Knolls of Wildermore, located north of Dunfast along the road. Horn desires to see the city of Byre Tor for himself and then to proceed on to the cave of which Nona spoke.\n2\tHorn and Gléowine want you to defeat Orcs in the city of Byre Tor. Gléowine desires to compose a song about Byre Tor, and is using your battles with Orcs as inspiration.\t\n3\tHorn and Gléowine want you to defeat Orcs in the city of Byre Tor. Gléowine desires to compose a song about Byre Tor, and is using your battles with Orcs as inspiration.\t\n4\tHorn and Gléowine want you to defeat Orcs in the city of Byre Tor. Gléowine desires to compose a song about Byre Tor, and is using your battles with Orcs as inspiration.\t\n5\tHorn and Gléowine want you to defeat Orcs in the city of Byre Tor. Gléowine desires to compose a song about Byre Tor, and is using your battles with Orcs as inspiration.\t\n6\tHorn and Gléowine want you to defeat Orcs in the city of Byre Tor. Gléowine desires to compose a song about Byre Tor, and is using your battles with Orcs as inspiration.\t\n7\tHorn and Gléowine want you to defeat Orcs in the city of Byre Tor. Gléowine desires to compose a song about Byre Tor, and is using your battles with Orcs as inspiration.\t\n8\tHorn and Gléowine want you to defeat Orcs in the city of Byre Tor. Gléowine desires to compose a song about Byre Tor, and is using your battles with Orcs as inspiration.\t\n9\tFind the entrance to Nona's cave in the High Knolls\tNona's cave is in the north-western heights of the rocky crags in the High Knolls, in Wildermore. Gléowine has finished his song, and Horn is satisfied with the Orcs you have defeated in Byre Tor.\n10\tSearch the cave for Nona\tIf this is the cave of which Nona spoke, she will likely be somewhere inside.\n11\tTalk to Elda\030Talk to Ymma\030Talk to the dying man\030Talk to Elfgifu\tThe survivors Nona rescued from Byre Tor can be found throughout the two chambers of her cave.\n12\tTalk to Nona\tNona is in her cave in the High Knolls.\n",
[1913]="7000B8DD\n1\tCollect Coveted Gem (total: 8)\tGoblin-town is located in the High Pass, high in the Misty Mountains, north-east of Rivendell. Merilos has asked you to journey into Goblin-town and reclaim a handful of coveted gems from the goblins there, while she works to repair the keys you found at Delossad.\n2\tBring gems to Merilos\tThe jeweller Merilos is at the Spire of Meeting, in Rivendell. You have acquired a handful of gems from the goblins of Goblin-town, as Merilos asked, and should return them now to her in exchange for the box of keys you left her to repair.\n",
[1914]="700378DF\n1\tTalk to Théoden in Meduseld\tThéoden King is inside the Golden Hall of Meduseld, in Edoras. Éowyn has asked you to see if the King has any further commands before he rides west to Isengard.\n2\tTalk to Théoden in Meduseld and watch his company ride to war\tThéoden King is inside the Golden Hall of Meduseld, in Edoras. The King is waiting to speak with you before he rides west, to Isengard and war.\n3\tTalk to Éowyn outside Meduseld, in Edoras\tÉowyn is outside the Golden Hall of Meduseld, in Edoras. The King and his company have left Edoras, and Éowyn is in charge of making ready the evacuation of the city.\n",
[1915]="7000B8DE\n1\tBring box of repaired keys to Candelleth\tCandelleth is at her Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen. Merilos has repaired as many of the keys as she was able, and you should bring them now to Candelleth.\n",
[1916]="7000B8DF\n1\tTalk to Muildir and uncover the secrets of Delossad\tMuildir is south-east of Echad Candelleth, outside the entrance to Delossad. Merilos has repaired the keys you found, and Candelleth asked you to show them to Muildir and delve into the secrets of Delossad in search of Narchuil.\n2\tTalk to Candelleth\tCandelleth is at her camp in Tâl Bruinen. You learned much within the depths of Delossad, but most worrisome is the troubling news that Mordrambor and the forces of Amarthiel have recovered Narchuil, her ring that was lost.\n",
[1917]="7000B8E0\n1\tBring rotted diary to Elrond\tElrond is in the library of Rivendell. Candelleth has asked you to bring Elrond the dire tidings that Angmar has recovered Narchuil.\n",
[1918]="700369BB\n1\tTalk to Horn in Nona's Cave in the High Knolls of Wildermore\tYour companions are in Nona's Cave in the High Knolls of Wildermore. Horn wishes to speak with you about the road ahead.\n2\tTalk to Corudan in Nona's Cave\030Talk to Gléowine in Nona's Cave\tCorudan is in Nona's Cave in the High Knolls, in Wildermore. Horn has asked you to speak with Corudan and Gléowine about the course he has suggested.\n3\tTalk to Horn in Nona's Cave\tHorn is in Nona's Cave in the High Knolls, in Wildermore. You have spoken with Gléowine and Corudan, and now Horn is waiting to see if you will accompany him to Edoras.\n4\tTalk to Hunbald at the Entwade, in the Sutcrofts\tHunbald is at Entwade, the Entwash Crossing in the Sutcrofts. Horn has resolved to return to Edoras, against the commands of the King. You, Horn, and Gléowine should present yourselves to Hunbald with this decision.\n",
[1919]="7000B8A0\n1\tTalk to Torogethir\030Talk to Galthoniel\tTorogethir is at a small camp just west of the Evendim Gate to the Fields of Fornost, north-east of Tinnudir. Galthoniel has a camp on a small rise overlooking the Barandalf, south-east of Tinnudir and east of the Shire-village of Dwaling. Calenglad has asked you to bring news of possible movements of the Angmarim out of Evendim to Torogethir and Galthoniel, the Rangers tasked with guarding the roads.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. You have told what Calenglad has guessed of Amarthiel's plans to the Rangers Torogethir and Galthoniel, and they will remain vigilant for any sign of Angmarim moving out of Evendim.\n",
[1920]="700377D5\n1\tRide to the barrows outside the entrance to Edoras\tThe barrows outside the entrance to Edoras will be a good place to meet up with your companions. Hunbald has allowed you to cross the Entwash, and now you should ride to the entrance of Edoras.\n2\tTalk to Horn by the barrows outside the entrance to Edoras\tHorn is by the barrows outside the entrance to Edoras. You have arrived at Edoras, and should speak now to Horn by the barrows.\n3\tMake your way into Edoras and meet up with Gléowine\tYou have come to Edoras and should now make your way up through the city.\n4\tTalk to Gléowine in Edoras, along the road\tGléowine is on the road within the entrance to Edoras, by a majestic white horse.\n5\tClimb the streets of Edoras to reach the entrance to Meduseld\tThe time has come to climb the streets of Edoras to the entrance to the Golden Hall of Meduseld, there to await the judgement of Théoden.\n6\tTalk to Háma outside the Golden Hall of Meduseld\tHáma stands before you, and he bars the way to the Golden Hall of Meduseld.\n",
})
